# `.beads/issues.jsonl` is a passive export of the issue database, regenerated
# and staged by `.githooks/pre-commit` on every commit — so every branch touches
# it, and every merge of two branches that moved the backlog used to stop on it
# and ask a human which side to keep. Neither side is the answer: issue data is
# merged in Dolt by `bd dolt pull`, never here, and this file only ever restates
# whatever the database already says. So the one correct resolution is to
# regenerate it, and that is what the driver does.
#
# The driver is per-clone git config — `make hooks` installs it, beside
# `core.hooksPath`. A clone without `bd` gets no driver and the conflict comes
# back as an ordinary one, which is the honest degrade: without the database
# there is nothing authoritative to regenerate from.
#
# Known and deliberate: the driver runs DURING the git merge, which is before
# `.githooks/post-merge` runs `bd dolt pull`. So the file in a merge commit
# restates the local database, not the merged one, and can lag by exactly one
# commit — the next `git commit` regenerates it from the pulled database. That
# is no worse than a human picking a side, because the database is the truth in
# both cases; it is written down so nobody reads the merge commit as a
# statement about the shared backlog.
.beads/issues.jsonl merge=beads-export
